            <ArticleTitle>Temporomandibular joint arthrography: comparison of morbidity with ionic and low osmolality contrast media.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>245-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We compared patient morbidity associated with temporomandibular joint (TMJ) arthrography using both meglumine/sodium diatrizoate (60%) and the new monoacidic dimer, Hexabrix, in a double-blind randomized clinical trial in 31 patients. Patients experienced maximal discomfort from TMJ arthrography with the initial joint filling and joint distension; this rapidly resolved over 10 minutes. Delayed exacerbation of pain is less than described for shoulder arthrography. The newer contrast media promise to decrease patient morbidity with arthrography.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
